/*
	RMSTEST 2 — what does circle_radius 0 actually do?

	guide:844 says "0 will disable circle_radius" and guide:842 documents the
	argument range as 1-50, so 0 is out of range AND documented as meaningful.
	docs/preview-design.md Sec.6.6... Sec.6.1 infers that "disable" means fall
	back to the default unconstrained ring (radius ~40% of map width, variance
	~20). That is an INFERENCE, not guide text, and the spec leans on it hard:
	it warns that reading 0 as a literal radius "stacks every player on the map
	center, which is both a visible lie and a guaranteed originFallbackCenter
	storm".

	Also worth knowing: language.json declares circle_radius's radiusPercent as
	min 1, so validate() will flag this legal script when it ships.

	HOW IT DISCRIMINATES
	Player lands are grass islands on a water base, so their positions are
	unmistakable on the minimap with no terrain noise.

	READ IT LIKE THIS
	  Islands in a wide ring, roughly 40% of map width from centre
	      -> "disable" = fall back to the default ring. Sec.6.1 confirmed.
	  Islands piled on/near the map centre, possibly overlapping
	      -> 0 is taken as a literal radius. Sec.6.1 is WRONG.
	  Islands scattered with no ring structure at all
	      -> "disable" = position like a neutral land (cross-shaped random
	         area). Sec.6.1 is WRONG in a different way, and this is the
	         reading its own wording ("disables circular positioning
	         entirely") most naturally suggests.

	RUN ON: Tiny, 8 players. Maximum players makes the ring shape obvious.
*/

<PLAYER_SETUP>
random_placement

<LAND_GENERATION>
base_terrain WATER

create_player_lands
{
	terrain_type GRASS
	base_size 6
	number_of_tiles 150
	circle_radius 0
}
